+
+### 2.1 Minimal assumptions for theory to be defensible
+We do *not* claim the full spiked-Wishart theory holds for equities. We claim:
+- High-dimensional regime: \(p/T\) non-negligible within windows
+- Within-window observations are “close enough” to elliptical / weak dependence *after*:
+  - factor prewhitening (optional) and/or
+  - robust scatter (Tyler/Huber) + clipping (winsor/huber)
+- Manufactured balanced design is *approximately* exchangeable within groups
+- Thresholds come from **synthetic null-FPR calibration** and are **not tuned on the same real windows**
+- Gating is conservative: overlay is *rare* and attributable
+
+### 2.2 High-risk approximations (must be acknowledged in paper)
+- time-series dependence (vol clustering, autocorr) violates MP/Wishart assumptions
+- “balanced design” via DoW/vol grouping is not structural and can be regime-correlated
+- stacking overlay with eigen-shrinkage (RIE/OAS) may double-correct
+
+**Operational mitigation story (must be empirically demonstrated):**
+- robustness knobs (Tyler/Huber, prewhitening) reduce sensitivity to violations
+- calibration stress tests show transfer does not catastrophically break under dependence/heavy tails
+
+---
+
+## 3) What makes this publishable (minimum package)
+
+### 3.1 Minimal publishable experimental claim (positive or clean-negative)
+
+**Option 1 — Positive result (ideal):**
+- On daily DoW design, overlay improves ΔQLIKE and/or ΔMSE vs at least **OAS** and **RIE**,
+- with controlled acceptance rate and no crisis blowups,
+- and mechanism is explained (why it helps when it helps).
+
+**Option 2 — Clean negative result (acceptable if well executed):**
+- Overlay does *not* improve and often harms when stacked with shrinkers,
+- we diagnose the mechanism via per-window forensics,
+- we show gating + calibration can keep harm bounded (especially in crisis),
+- we present a clear “when not to use” conclusion with reproducible evidence.
+
+### 3.2 Minimal designs/regimes/estimators required
+**Paper v1 (minimum):**
+- Designs: `dow` (required); `vol` only if design_ok rate is stable (>=70% of windows)
+- Estimators: {SCM, OAS, RIE} × {overlay off/on}
+- Edge modes: `scm` (required); `tyler` (recommended robustness check)
+- Prewhitening: off (required); FF5+MOM on (recommended)
+- Portfolios: EW + MV (box + ridge; solver behavior must be explicit)
+- Regimes: calm vs crisis slice (must report acceptance + deltas by regime)
+
+### 3.3 Kill criteria (when we pivot)
+We pivot away from “finance-first improvement paper” if:
+- after **mechanism forensics + overlay-vs-shrinker ablation**, overlay is consistently harmful or null across SCM *and* hurts under robust/whitened variants, *and*
+- acceptance remains too low to matter (<1% changed windows) without violating null-FPR.
+
+Pivot options (pre-approved):
+- **Pivot A:** Paper v1 = daily one-way only + “safety + when it helps/harms”
+- **Pivot B:** Stats paper: robust MP-edge detection under heavy tails/dependence (finance as application)
+- **Pivot C:** Applied paper: operational portfolio impact + crisis safety, not mean ΔMSE headline
+
